.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
data/raw/
data/history/
data/live/
# v12 W4 §5.1: `gaffer core-insights` writes one parquet per season per table
# here. Collected data, not source — ignored now rather than at the end of the
# workstream, because the command is runnable today.
data/core_insights/
models/*.joblib
models/*.json
reports/*.html
reports/*.json
logs/
.DS_Store
.superpowers/
# Build output of frontend/ (`npm run build`); the wheel ships it via the
# hatch `artifacts` entry, so nothing in here is tracked — not even a
# placeholder, which every build with emptyOutDir would delete again. A clone
# without it serves the "frontend not built" 503 until you build.
src/gaffer/web/static/
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
reports/
.claude/
config.toml
# v12 W5 §6.2: the overlay the Settings tab writes. Untracked for the same
# reason config.toml is — it is one machine's own answers, not the project's.
config.local.toml
# v12 W4 §5.4: the hand-edited set-piece override. One user's knowledge about
# one season, so it is untracked; the template ships as a package asset
# (src/gaffer/assets/set_pieces.example.toml) so a fresh clone still has one.
data/set_pieces.toml
